  "summary": "Oakland's planned 300-camera Flock Safety ALPR network, approved by City Council in October 2023, will be operated by the California Highway Patrol rather than Oakland police. Privacy advocates raise concerns about CHP's longer 60-day data retention period versus Oakland's 30-day policy and the fact that Oakland's surveillance ordinance won't apply to CHP.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Operations and installation management for the plate reader and camera investment announced in 2023 will be managed under this effort, and most directly by CHP",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "If they go 60 days, that means more accumulation of data, which would make the system more invasive from a privacy perspective",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "Hofer pointed out that Oakland's surveillance ordinance wouldn't apply to CHP, and the agency doesn't have to give the city updates about its surveillance activities",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
